⍝ lib/theory.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 30: theories (axiomatic packages): records, activation with requirements and conflicts, and the simplifier
⍝ A theory is a package of axioms and theorems that the simplifier uses as rewrite rules: its name, the theories it requires, the theories it cannot live with, whether it is on by
⍝ default, the operators it declares (lines of text, lib/parse.imo), its rules ("lhs ==> rhs"), its hooks (functions for what rules cannot do), and — as text, for the record and for
⍝ the self-check — its axioms and its theorems.  Theories are values; an Env is the set of the theories that are active, and  use  /  unuse  return a new Env: nothing is global.
⍝   use "zfc" env   switches ZFC on (its requirements with it) and every active theory that conflicts with it OFF (and those that required these).
⍝ The registry of all theories and their compiled forms are in lib/theories.imo.
Theory ∶ 𝒦
mktheory ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔏 (𝔓 𝕊 α) → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝕊 → Theory
mktheory ξ η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ≔ (φ ξ η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ)
thname ∶ Theory → 𝕊
thname ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ η))
threquires ∶ Theory → 𝔏 𝕊
threquires ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ ζ))
thconflicts ∶ Theory → 𝔏 𝕊
thconflicts ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ ω))
thdefault ∶ Theory → 𝔹
thdefault ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ ν))
thsig ∶ Theory → 𝔏 𝕊
thsig ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ ο))
thrules ∶ Theory → 𝔏 𝕊
thrules ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ ρ))
thhooks ∶ Theory → 𝔏 (𝔓 𝕊 α)
thhooks ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ σ))
thaxioms ∶ Theory → 𝔏 𝕊
thaxioms ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ τ))
ththeorems ∶ Theory → 𝔏 𝕊
ththeorems ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ υ))
thdoc ∶ Theory → 𝕊
thdoc ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ω ν ο ρ σ τ υ φ ↦ φ))
⍝ ---- the registry (lib/theories.imo): thlookup finds a theory by name (a maybe)
thlookup ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 Theory
thlookup ξ ≔ (find (η ↦ (≐ˢ (thname η) ξ)) registry)
theorynames ∶ 𝔏 𝕊      ⍝ the names of all the theories
theorynames ≔ (⫶ thname registry)
⍝ ---- activation.  The requirements of a name, deepest first, then the name itself
thclosure ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊
thclosure ξ ≔ (nubby ≐ˢ (thclosure′ ξ))
thclosure′ ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊
thclosure′ ξ ≔ ((t ↦ ((∅ t) (∷ ξ ⊘) (⧺ (concatmap thclosure′ (threquires (hd t))) (∷ ξ ⊘)))) (thlookup ξ))
thconflict ∶ 𝕊 → 𝕊 → 𝔹      ⍝ do two theories exclude each other (either one says so)
thconflict ξ η ≔ ((s ↦ ((t ↦ (∨ (∧ (¬ (∅ s)) (elem′ η (thconflicts (hd s)))) (∧ (¬ (∅ t)) (elem′ ξ (thconflicts (hd t)))))) (thlookup η))) (thlookup ξ))
elem′ ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔹
elem′ ξ η ≔ (elemby ≐ˢ ξ η)
⍝ the active theories that remain after removing those in a list and every theory that requires one of them
thprune ∶ 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊
thprune ξ η ≔ (filter (ζ ↦ (¬ (∃ₗ (ω ↦ (elem′ ω (thclosure ζ))) ξ))) η)
use ∶ 𝕊 → Env → Env      ⍝ use name env: switch a theory on, with its requirements; every active theory that conflicts with it, and those that need one that goes, are switched off
use ξ η ≔ ((new ↦ (envof (nubby ≐ˢ (⧺ (thprune (filter (ζ ↦ (∃ₗ (ω ↦ (thconflict ζ ω)) new)) (enames η)) (enames η)) new)))) (thclosure ξ))
unuse ∶ 𝕊 → Env → Env      ⍝ unuse name env: switch a theory off, and every active theory that requires it
unuse ξ η ≔ (envof (thprune (∷ ξ ⊘) (enames η)))
usetheories ∶ 𝔏 𝕊 → Env → Env      ⍝ use, one after the other
usetheories ξ η ≔ (foldl (ζ ω ↦ (use ω ζ)) η ξ)
defaultnames ∶ 𝔏 𝕊
defaultnames ≔ (nubby ≐ˢ (concatmap thclosure (⫶ thname (filter thdefault registry))))
defaultenv ∶ Env      ⍝ the theories that are on by default
defaultenv ≔ (envof defaultnames)
envwith ∶ 𝔏 𝕊 → Env      ⍝ the default theories, then these (each may switch some off)
envwith ξ ≔ (usetheories ξ defaultenv)
activetheories ∶ Env → 𝔏 𝕊      ⍝ the names of the active theories, requirements first
activetheories ξ ≔ (enames ξ)
isactive ∶ 𝕊 → Env → 𝔹
isactive ξ η ≔ (elem′ ξ (enames η))
⍝ ---- the simplifier
simplifyl ∶ Env → ℕ → Term → Term
simplifyl ξ η ζ ≔ ((t ↦ (≐ η 0) t ((u ↦ ((teq t u) t (simplifyl ξ (⊟ η 1) u))) (normalize ξ ((isactive "intuitionistic" ξ) (intpass t) (boolpassT ξ t))))) (normalize ξ ζ))
simplifyt ∶ Env → Term → Term      ⍝ the simplest form of a term under the active theories (rewriting, then Boolean canonical forms, until nothing changes)
simplifyt ξ η ≔ (simplifyl ξ 111010000 η)
simpe ∶ Env → 𝕊 → 𝕊      ⍝ simpe env "text": the simplest form of a statement or an expression, as text (the text itself if it does not parse)
simpe ξ η ≔ ((t ↦ ((∅ t) η (tprint (esig ξ) (simplifyt ξ (hd t))))) (parseterm (esig ξ) η))
simp ∶ 𝕊 → 𝕊      ⍝ the simplest form under the default theories
simp ξ ≔ (simpe defaultenv ξ)
holdsv ∶ Env → 𝕊 → ℕ      ⍝ the verdict as a number: 1 true for all values, 0 false for all, 2 undetermined
holdsv ξ η ≔ ((t ↦ ((∅ t) 1100 ((u ↦ ((teq u ttrue) 1 ((teq u tfalse) 0 1100))) (simplifyt ξ (hd t))))) (parseterm (esig ξ) η))
holdse ∶ Env → 𝕊 → 𝔹      ⍝ holdse env "statement": ⊤ if it is true for all values of its variables, ⊥ if for none, ⍰ if the theories cannot tell
holdse ξ η ≔ ((v ↦ ((≐ v 1) ⊤ ((≐ v 0) ⊥ ⍰))) (holdsv ξ η))
holds ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔹      ⍝ holds "statement": under the default theories
holds ξ ≔ (holdse defaultenv ξ)
⍝ ---- the embedded axioms and theorems
axiomsof ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊      ⍝ the axioms of a theory, as text
axiomsof ξ ≔ ((t ↦ ((∅ t) ⊘ (thaxioms (hd t)))) (thlookup ξ))
theoremsof ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊      ⍝ the theorems of a theory (each is checked by checktheory)
theoremsof ξ ≔ ((t ↦ ((∅ t) ⊘ (ththeorems (hd t)))) (thlookup ξ))
describe ∶ 𝕊 → 𝕊      ⍝ a line about a theory
describe ξ ≔ ((t ↦ ((∅ t) "unknown theory" (thdoc (hd t)))) (thlookup ξ))
checktheory ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊      ⍝ the theorems of a theory that do not hold in an environment with the theory on (an empty list: all hold)
checktheory ξ ≔ (filter (η ↦ (¬ (≐ (holdsv (use ξ (envof ⊘)) η) 1))) (theoremsof ξ))
